  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">for Reimagining the Role of Data for Foreign Assistance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AidData is a research lab at the College of William and Mary that generates evidence to help decision makers design, implement, and evaluate policies that improve the well-being of people living in low- and middle-income countries. This grant supports a new program that will identify persistent gaps in the supply and demand for key development data assets, which development data systems need to be preserved and protected, and which ones need to be redesigned and reinvented.</narrative>
  </description>
